# Citation metadata for FST4 in the Citation File Format (CFF 1.2.0). GitHub
# renders it as "Cite this repository"; README.md ("Citing FST4") states the same.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If FST4 contributes to your research, please cite the toolbox paper given
  under preferred-citation. Work that uses the budgeted stochastic (sampled)
  sequential search should also cite the preprint listed under references.
type: software
title: "Feature Selection Toolbox 4 (FST4)"
abstract: >-
  A standalone C++17 header-only library and command-line tool for feature
  selection and, more generally, for finding near-optimal or provably optimal
  subsets of a large finite set under any subset-quality criterion. Criteria:
  built-in filters (normal and multinomial model based) and wrappers over
  deterministic classifiers and regressors, or a user-supplied set function,
  including one computed by an external program. Searches: optimal Branch &
  Bound and exhaustive search, sequential, floating, oscillating and budgeted
  stochastic search, with result trackers for stability and similarity
  evaluation. Deterministic and bit-identical at any thread count.
version: 4.2.0
license: AGPL-3.0-only
url: "https://fst.utia.cz"
repository-code: "https://github.com/psomol/fst4"
keywords:
  - feature selection
  - subset selection
  - variable selection
  - combinatorial optimization
  - set function optimization
  - black-box optimization
  - dimensionality reduction
  - pattern recognition
  - machine learning
  - branch and bound
  - floating search
  - C++
authors:
  - family-names: Somol
    given-names: Petr
    email: somol@utia.cas.cz
    affiliation: >-
      Institute of Information Theory and Automation of the Czech Academy of
      Sciences (ÚTIA), Prague
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "Feature Selection Toolbox"
  authors:
    - family-names: Somol
      given-names: Petr
    - family-names: Pudil
      given-names: Pavel
  journal: "Pattern Recognition"
  volume: 35
  issue: 12
  start: 2749
  end: 2759
  year: 2002
  doi: 10.1016/S0031-3203(01)00245-X
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Stochastic Sequential Search in Very-High-Dimensional Feature Selection"
    authors:
      - family-names: Somol
        given-names: Petr
      - family-names: Grim
        given-names: Jiri
    year: 2026
    url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.01502"
    identifiers:
      - type: other
        value: "arXiv:2608.01502"
        description: "arXiv preprint (cs.LG)"
    notes: >-
      Describes the budgeted stochastic (sampled) sequential search
      (fst4 --evaluator sampled; demos/demo36.cfg and demos/demo37t.cfg), a
      new principal component of FST4 and one of the main contributions of
      this release; it does not describe the toolbox as a whole.
